\title{Datalog queries}
\import{base-macros}
\tag{feature-demo}

\p{
  Forester carries a Datalog engine over the forest's relational graph: links,
  transclusions, authorship, taxa, and tags all become facts you can query at
  \em{build time}. Wrapping a query in \code{query} materializes the matches
  inline. The query below finds every tree tagged \code{feature-demo} — that is,
  the other pages of this very gallery — and lists them live:
}

\query{
  \datalog{
    ?X -: {\rel/has-tag ?X '{feature-demo}}
  }
}

\p{
  The premise is a relation applied to terms: the variable \code{?X} is a bare,
  space-separated term, and \code{{feature-demo}} is a content constant
  (tick-quoted). Built-in relations include \code{is-reference}, \code{is-person},
  \code{has-taxon}, \code{has-tag}, \code{links-to}, and \code{transcludes} (plus
  its transitive closure) queries also compose negated premises after \code{#}
  for set-difference selection.
}
